faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
A full four-phase sweep of the simple_bgp lab found no fault. Phase 1 reachability showed 0% loss in both directions (pc1→pc2 and pc2→pc1). Phase A infrastructure checks confirmed all interfaces are UP with no carrier transitions (carrier counter = 0 on every interface, including the inter-router router1:eth0 ↔ router2:eth0 link), no ACL rules, no duplicate MACs, and correct addressing on all hosts. Phase B control-plane checks confirmed FRR is healthy on both routers, BGP sessions are Established using standard default timers (180 s hold / 60 s keepalive), ASNs and prefix advertisements are correct, and no qdisc shaping exists. The FRR BGP log records a single clean session establishment at 13:09:31 followed by uninterrupted keepalive exchanges every 60 seconds — no NOTIFICATION messages, no Idle/Active state transitions, and no session drops. The in-memory FRR counter "Connections established: 1; dropped: 0" confirms the session has never been torn down since startup. No flap script, stress tool, or cron job was found on either router. The user's complaint of "every few minutes the session resets" describes a past intermittent event, but no mechanism capable of producing it — link flap, BGP timer misconfiguration, authentication failure, BFD, flap script, ACL injection, or resource exhaustion — is present in the live lab. The claim is unconfirmed by any trace or mechanism. The network is operating correctly.
=== END ===